        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-12T13:49:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I\u0027m missing something fundamental here.\n\nWe need to make sure the limit is never exceeded. I thought we\u0027d be dividing the limit by the number of providers and have each provider limit by that. In this picture there is no iface. In this world I don\u0027t understand why this function takes an interface.\n\nSo assuming I\u0027m missing a fundamental reason that this must take an interface, that means we can\u0027t do what I describe above. Instead we need to divide by the number of interfaces then right ? But if that\u0027s the case, if 2 providers track the same interface, we can have overages. E.g. limit is 1MB and there is only 1 interface on the system tracked by 2 providers, we set the limit to 1MB because 1MB / 1 \u003d 1MB, and both providers do 999kB and we have exceeded the limit.\n\nWhat am I missing ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1505,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 1505,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a0610216a33db6a192c2ac2cad550fb960f9c0e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
